  "instance_name": "racial_justification_of_death_as_crime",
  "label": "The act of justifying death as a crime based on racial stereotypes or prejudices",
  "description": "Racial justification of death as a crime refers to the act of justifying death as a crime based on racial stereotypes or prejudices, often by implying that the victims are not human or that their death is not a serious issue. In the meme, the implication that killing zombies (non-human entities) is not homicide is used to justify racially motivated death as a crime. This requires understanding of the concept of racial justification of death as a crime and its role in promoting harmful ideologies.",
